cmrgo4mrk003m5voxj9mya9z4	cmrgo4mr400375voxjwil72aj	How GitHub gave every repository a durable owner	How GitHub gave every repository a durable owner\nGitHub has over 14,000 repositories across our primary internal GitHub organization. As of early 2025, there were over 11,000 non-archived repositories, the vast majority of which with no clear owner. For repositories attached to production services, we have historically had robust durable ownership, but for repositories with no associated service, there was no reliable way to tell who the owner is. That gap became a recurring problem during our secret scanning remediation effort: while we could technically rotate a secret, doing so without knowing the repository owner was risky and often disruptive, and we had no clear way to route remediation work. Over the course of a month and a half, we validated ownership for every active repository, archived about 8,000 repositories that were no lon	\N	\N	EXTRACTED	2026-07-11 17:58:38.912	2026-07-11 18:00:59.855	Developer Tools	case-study	{GitHub,Kubernetes,Datadog}	Implemented ownership model	{"Repo Ownership","GitHub App"}	Repository Management	GitHub addressed the issue of unowned repositories by creating a new ownership model that ensures every active repository is assigned a validated owner. This change was prompted by challenges in secret scanning remediation when the ownership was unclear. By implementing custom properties for ownership and automating the process, GitHub archived 11,000 unused repositories and ensured that every active repo has defined ownership. Moving forward, the model will enforce ownership at repository creation to maintain consistency. This initiative strengthens governance and enhances workflow efficiency across the organization.
cmrgo4laj000x5voxy6u9w905	cmrgo4l9a000i5voxvtvi20gq	Making AI search smarter	Making AI search smarter\nSearch drives most experiences on the web. It's how we get things done, and how nearly everything on the web gets found — the creators, the merchants, the answer to whatever you just typed into a box. For nearly 30 years, that discovery journey ran on a simple bargain: let a search engine crawl your content, and it sends you visitors. You turned those visitors into a business — through ads, subscriptions, or just the audience itself. Being discoverable and getting paid were the same thing. A year ago, on the first Content Independence Day, we drew a line to defend that bargain in the AI era. But a line in the sand was only a first step. Since then, the prevalence of AI search in consumers’ lives has only accelerated as more than 50% of traffic online is non-human. The threat is no longer a	\N	\N	EXTRACTED	2026-07-11 17:58:37.003	2026-07-11 17:58:46.714	Web Development	announcement	{Cloudflare,Ceramic.ai,You.com,"Pew Research Center"}	launch new bot options	{"Pay Per Crawl","Pay Per Use","answer engine optimization (AEO)"}	AI Search	Today, Cloudflare announced new initiatives aimed at improving AI search and compensating content creators. With over 50% of online traffic being non-human, the traditional web model is challenged as AI search engines summarize content without driving traffic to original sources. To address this, Cloudflare introduces new bot options and transitions from 'Pay Per Crawl' to 'Pay Per Use', ensuring that creators are rewarded when their content is utilized. This move aims to enhance content discoverability, reduce unnecessary crawling, and establish a fair compensation model, supporting a more sustainable future for content creators in the evolving digital landscape.
cmrgo4lal00105vox5q6prji6	cmrgo4l98000g5vox90gw7nfs	Announcing the Monetization Gateway: charge for any resource behind Cloudflare via x402	Announcing the Monetization Gateway: charge for any resource behind Cloudflare via x402\nToday, we are announcing the Cloudflare Monetization Gateway, an engine that will give Cloudflare customers the ability to charge for any asset protected by Cloudflare: web pages, datasets, APIs, or MCP tools. It will provide a single control plane to manage payment policies and access controls across your applications, while also protecting your origin from high payment volumes by handling payment verification and enforcement at the edge. At launch, payments will settle in stablecoins over x402, the open protocol we are building with a coalition of more than 25 industry leaders via the x402 Foundation. The evolving business model of the web For 30 years, the web has run on a simple economic bargain: trading content for human attention. That attention has been monetized through advertising	\N	\N	EXTRACTED	2026-07-11 17:58:37.005	2026-07-11 17:58:50.868	Cloud	announcement	{Cloudflare,x402,"x402 Foundation","Open USD",USDC}	announce Monetization Gateway	{"Monetization Gateway"}	Payments Gateway	Cloudflare has announced the launch of the Monetization Gateway, enabling customers to monetize digital assets like web pages, APIs, and datasets. This gateway offers a unified control plane for payment policies and utilizes stablecoins for micropayments, leveraging the x402 open protocol for seamless transactions. This shift aims to transition the web towards usage-based pricing, allowing AI agents to make payments directly for resources. The Monetization Gateway enhances billing efficiency and addresses the growing need for automated transaction mechanisms in a changing digital landscape, paving the way for a new revenue model on the Internet.
cmrgo4lam00115voxoh0qf2y3	cmrgo4l96000e5voxdfdm0ahs	Cloudflare proudly joins the UK government's Cyber Resilience Pledge	Cloudflare proudly joins the UK government's Cyber Resilience Pledge\nToday, the UK government launched the Cyber Resilience Pledge: a voluntary framework inviting organizations to commit to foundational cybersecurity governance, board-level accountability, and comprehensive cybersecurity coverage across supply chains. Cloudflare is proud to join the pledge’s founding cohort of signatories and continue our long-standing work with the Department of Science, Innovation and Technology (DSIT), National Cyber Security Centre, and others to shape a more secure, future-ready digital economy for the UK. The pledge's core pillars — democratizing security, leadership accountability, and radical transparency — have been at the heart of Cloudflare since day one. Instead of approaching this framework as a new set of commitments to meet, we see it as a welcome validation 	\N	\N	EXTRACTED	2026-07-11 17:58:37.006	2026-07-11 17:59:08.216	Security	announcement	{Cloudflare,"Department of Science, Innovation and Technology","National Cyber Security Centre","Cyber Essentials","ISO 27001","SOC 2 Type II"}	launch Cyber Resilience Pledge	{"Cloudflare Access","Cloudflare Gateway"}	Cybersecurity Governance	The UK government has launched the Cyber Resilience Pledge, inviting organizations to commit to enhanced cybersecurity governance. Cloudflare is among the founding signatories of this framework, which emphasizes leadership accountability and comprehensive supply chain security. As cyber threats rise significantly, Cloudflare aims to align with the government's mission to elevate cybersecurity across various sectors. By adhering to this pledge, Cloudflare reinforces its commitment to help foster a more resilient digital economy in the UK, ensuring that all organizations, regardless of size, can participate in enhanced cybersecurity efforts.
cmrgo4my800485vox0llfd79s	cmrgo4mxx003v5voxr2x8sx52	Adopting AV1 for Real-Time Communication (RTC) at Scale	Adopting AV1 for Real-Time Communication (RTC) at Scale\nAdopting AV1 for real-time communication at Meta has been a multi-year effort spanning codec selection, device eligibility, rate control, and error resilience. We’re sharing the technical and operational challenges while deploying AV1 and expanding coverage, and how we addressed them for real-time communication. We’re presenting several technologies for improving AV1 call quality, including rate control and error resilience. The AV1 video codec, first standardized by AOMedia in 2018, has rapidly evolved and gained widespread industry support. Today, leading companies like YouTube, Netflix, and Meta stream video using AV1 at scale. Meta introduced AV1 for real-time video calls on high-end devices in 2023, aiming to deliver superior call quality. Since then, we have made notable progress in 	\N	\N	EXTRACTED	2026-07-11 17:58:39.152	2026-07-11 18:01:22.477	AI	analysis	{Meta,AV1,AOMedia,H.264/AVC,Messenger,WhatsApp,YouTube,Netflix,dav1d,"Pixel 8"}	adopting AV1 for RTC	{"Meta Real-Time Communication",Messenger,WhatsApp}	video codec	Meta has been implementing the AV1 video codec for real-time communication (RTC) over several years, focusing on codec selection, device eligibility, and error resilience. This transition enables better video quality using less bandwidth, crucial for users on slower networks. The adoption has improved call quality significantly, especially in bandwidth-constrained conditions. Meta employs a low-complexity encoder along with a machine learning framework to validate device compatibility and integrate AV1 into existing mobile apps. Looking ahead, Meta aims to extend AV1 support to group calls and enhance overall user experience across devices.
