cmrgo4uu4004o5voxcn3bpqt2	cmrgo4utl004d5vox60dgnak1	Meet Brain: The AI system behind Azure reliability	Meet Brain: The AI system behind Azure reliability\nIn this article How Azure's AI-powered reliability intelligence system works Why Brain is needed What is Brain? Azure’s centralized AIOps for cloud reliability Foundations of Azure’s digital twin for cloud health What it means to operate against a cloud intelligence system The future of agentic AI and cloud operations What's next for Azure reliability and Brain Azure reliability Takeaway: Brain is Azure’s AI-powered cloud reliability intelligence system: an AIOps system that sits as an intelligent layer on top of Azure Resource Graph and fuses platform telemetry, AI/ML models, service dependencies, and customer impact into a single, continuously updated view of how every service, region, and workload is performing. It already powers customer Azure resource health notifications, deployment 	\N	\N	EXTRACTED	2026-07-11 17:58:49.372	2026-07-11 18:01:32.038	Cloud	announcement	{Azure,"Azure Resource Graph",AI/ML,"agentic AI","Microsoft Research"}	introduce AI system	{Brain}	AIOps	Microsoft has introduced Brain, an AI-powered cloud reliability intelligence system that operates on top of Azure Resource Graph to enhance Azure reliability. By integrating platform telemetry, AI/ML models, and service dependencies, Brain provides a unified view of Azure's health and automates key reliability workflows, such as health notifications and outage declarations. This innovation addresses gaps in cloud reliability, enabling faster incident response and improved customer experience. As Azure continues to evolve, Brain serves as a foundational element for future advancements in cloud operations and reliability.
