cmrgo4l9v000v5voxzgr1vtt3	cmrgo4l94000b5voxx5b3t4yn	Improving Smart Tiered Cache for Public Cloud Regions	Improving Smart Tiered Cache for Public Cloud Regions\nIn 2021, we shipped Smart Tiered Cache. The idea: for each origin behind your site, Cloudflare picks the single best upper-tier data center to route through, based on real-time latency. Flip one switch, and we find the fastest path from our network to your origin. That works as long as an origin IP lives in one fixed place. Public cloud origins usually don't. They sit behind anycast or regional unicast front ends, so one origin IP can look equally close to a dozen Cloudflare data centers at once — and the latency probes have nothing to lock onto. Smart Tiered Cache handles this the safe way: when there's no clear winner, it falls back to several upper tiers. Nothing breaks. You just lose the thing that made a single closest tier worth it, which is cache efficiency. Smart Tiered Cache for P	\N	\N	EXTRACTED	2026-07-11 17:58:36.979	2026-07-11 17:58:40.782	Cloud	update	{Cloudflare,AWS,GCP,Azure,"Oracle Cloud"}	launch Smart Tiered Cache improvements	{"Smart Tiered Cache"}	Caching	Cloudflare has updated its Smart Tiered Cache to better handle origins hosted on public clouds that utilize anycast IPs. By allowing users to set a region hint, Cloudflare optimizes latency by accurately mapping cloud origins to their respective regions. This enhancement helps avoid latency issues associated with hairpin traffic, improving cache efficiency. The update is available for all Cloudflare customers, enhancing the user experience for those utilizing cloud services. Cloudflare continues to expand support for more providers and origin setups.
cmrgo4lai000w5voxxz2ozpdl	cmrgo4l99000h5vox3dwbbvdg	Content Independence Day, one year on: building the business model for the agentic Internet	Content Independence Day, one year on: building the business model for the agentic Internet\nOne year ago, we declared Content Independence Day. At the time, we could see what many in the industry were beginning to sense: the fundamental economics of the Internet were shifting. AI adoption was accelerating, publishers were experiencing rapid declines in referral traffic, and AI companies were crawling the web at unprecedented scale, often without clearly declaring intent, and almost always without compensation. We changed the defaults. For all new domains on Cloudflare, AI training crawlers would be blocked by default unless domain owners chose otherwise. We didn't do this to wall off the web. We did it because we believed a healthier ecosystem required transparency, control, scarcity, and ultimately, a market where high-quality content could be valued and exchanged fairly. A year	\N	\N	EXTRACTED	2026-07-11 17:58:37.002	2026-07-11 17:58:41.277	AI	analysis	{Cloudflare,AI,LLMs,Google}	Share report	{}	Content Monetization	One year after declaring Content Independence Day, Cloudflare reports significant changes in the Internet's economic landscape due to rapid AI adoption. With more than 50% of online traffic now non-human, traditional content discovery and monetization models are breaking down. Publishers face declining referral traffic, prompting a shift towards a licensing economy for content. The report emphasizes the need for transparency, control for site owners, and the creation of a marketplace between content creators and AI companies, suggesting that evolving infrastructure is essential for a sustainable future in the agentic Internet.
